WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:07.000
There are three kinds of products for vectors:
the dot product and the cross product

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.016
of two vectors, and the scalar triple product
of

3
00:00:10.016 --> 00:00:12.780
three vectors. Today we will look at the dot

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:18.580
product of vectors. Why is the dot product
called a scalar product,

5
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:25.340
and what is a scalar? It is a number. The dot
product of vectors is also

6
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.250
a number. The dot product of vectors a and b

7
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.147
is the product of the lengths of these vectors

8
00:00:33.147 --> 00:00:35.730
and the cosine of the angle between them.

9
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:43.040
The dot product formula can be written as
follows. The angle between vectors a

10
00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:49.410
and b is denoted by the Greek letter φ.

11
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.620
The dot product can be written in the
following form.

12
00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:59.400
Let us consider the following equalities. The
product of the length of vector a

13
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:06.200
and the cosine of the angle between vectors a
and b

14
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.000
equals the projection of vector a onto vector
b.

15
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.642
Similarly, the product of the length of vector

16
00:01:14.642 --> 00:01:17.930
b and the cosine of the angle between a and b

17
00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:24.730
equals the projection of vector b onto vector
a.

18
00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:29.060
These two equalities give the following one:

19
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:35.960
to find the dot product of two vectors,
multiply the magnitude of one of them

20
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.180
by the projection of the other onto it.

21
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:46.540
Let us look at the properties of the dot
product. Property one:

22
00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:51.700
the dot product of a vector with itself is
called its scalar square.

23
00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:58.390
Property two: the dot product is commutative.

24
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.842
Property three: with respect to a scalar
factor,

25
00:02:02.842 --> 00:02:06.140
the dot product has the following property.

26
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:13.200
Property four: the dot product is
distributive.

27
00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:20.320
The last, fifth property: if the dot product
of vectors a and b is zero,

28
00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:27.040
the vectors are perpendicular. That is, the
dot product of two vectors

29
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:33.540
equals zero if the vectors are orthogonal, or
perpendicular.

30
00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:40.660
Let us look at an example of finding a dot
product. Let the lengths of vectors a and

31
00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:47.620
b be given, and let the angle between the
vectors be sixty degrees.

32
00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:51.083
We substitute the given values into the dot
product

33
00:02:51.083 --> 00:02:53.910
formula. Since the cosine of sixty degrees

34
00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:59.590
equals one half, the value of the expression
is nine.

35
00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.888
Now let us look at an example that uses the
properties

36
00:03:05.888 --> 00:03:08.850
of the dot product. Find the dot product of 3a

37
00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:16.910
minus 2b and 5a minus 6b, if

38
00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:23.920
the length of vector a is four, the length of
vector b is six, and

39
00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:30.630
the angle between the vectors is π/3. Let us
expand the brackets

40
00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.330
in this dot product.

41
00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:38.620
Using the properties of the dot product, we
get the following expression.

42
00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:45.290
Substituting the given numbers into the
expression, we get three hundred thirty-six.

43
00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:50.261
The dot product can be computed from the
coordinates

44
00:03:50.261 --> 00:03:52.900
of the vectors. Let vectors a and b

45
00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.620
be given.

46
00:03:55.100 --> 00:04:01.620
Then their dot product is found by the
following formula, that is,

47
00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.487
the dot product equals the sum of the products
of

48
00:04:04.487 --> 00:04:07.120
the corresponding coordinates of the vectors.

49
00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:13.120
The dot product lets us find the basic metric
quantities.

50
00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:16.300
In particular, we can compute angles.

51
00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:19.842
The cosine of the angle between two vectors is
defined

52
00:04:19.842 --> 00:04:22.860
as the ratio of the dot product of the vectors

53
00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:27.390
to the product of their lengths.

54
00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:33.700
We can also find the value of the projection
of one vector onto another.

55
00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:37.080
The projection of a vector onto a vector
equals

56
00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.080
the ratio of the dot product of the vectors

57
00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:45.040
to the magnitude, or length, of the vector
being projected onto.

58
00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:51.022
Let us look at an example. Vectors a and b are
given,

59
00:04:51.022 --> 00:04:54.140
and we need to find the angle between them.

60
00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.940
Let us write the vectors in coordinate form.

61
00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:02.118
We substitute the coordinates into the formula
for

62
00:05:02.118 --> 00:05:05.250
the angle between vectors. The calculation

63
00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:12.050
gives the fraction seventeen fiftieths. Then
the angle φ equals the arccosine

64
00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.770
of seventeen fiftieths.

65
00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:21.220
Let us look at one more example: for what
value of m are the vectors a and

66
00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:24.613
b perpendicular? We substitute the coordinates
into

67
00:05:24.613 --> 00:05:27.740
the perpendicularity condition for two
vectors.

68
00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:34.740
We get an equation with the unknown m. After
simplifying,

69
00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:42.100
m equals six. So, if the x-coordinate of
vector a

70
00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:48.530
equals six, vectors a and b are perpendicular.

71
00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:56.420
Along with adding vectors and multiplying a
vector by a number,

72
00:05:56.420 --> 00:06:03.240
the dot product of two vectors plays an
important role. In this lesson

73
00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:09.970
we learned what the dot product of vectors is,
looked at its properties,

74
00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:16.350
and worked through typical problems on
computing the dot product in detail.
